WEBVTT

00:00:00.750 --> 00:00:04.460
Episode 3

00:00:00.750 --> 00:00:04.460
Yamato Takes Off!!
The 296,000 Light Years Challenge!!

00:00:00.750 --> 00:00:04.460
( Air date: Oct 20, 1974 )

00:00:35.930 --> 00:00:40.180
Space Battleship

00:00:35.930 --> 00:00:40.180
<i>YAMATO</i>

00:01:35.700 --> 00:01:44.600
In 2199, the mysterious Gamilus fleet
came from the large Magellanic Cloud...

00:01:44.600 --> 00:01:47.910
...established a frontline base on
Pluto, and began attacking Earth.

00:01:50.320 --> 00:01:53.350
Earth's surface was contaminated
by radioactive poison...

00:01:53.350 --> 00:01:55.930
...and mankind was
driven underground.

00:01:57.930 --> 00:02:02.990
And the radioactive poison from the
meteor bombs has reached underground.

00:02:02.990 --> 00:02:07.300
Humanity has only one year
left until it becomes extinct.

00:02:06.150 --> 00:02:08.750
Galactic System

00:02:09.030 --> 00:02:14.860
Meanwhile, Queen Starsha of Iscandar, who is
also located in the large Magellanic Cloud...

00:02:11.850 --> 00:02:14.650
Magellanic Cloud

00:02:14.860 --> 00:02:17.310
...has sent a message
to help Earth.

00:02:17.090 --> 00:02:19.950
Planet Gamilus

00:02:17.090 --> 00:02:19.950
Planet Iscandar

00:02:20.470 --> 00:02:25.600
The Cosmo Cleaner-D, which can eliminate the radioactive poison, is on Iscandar.

00:02:25.600 --> 00:02:28.300
Once it is obtained,
Earth can be saved.

00:02:30.160 --> 00:02:35.810
Secretly undergoing conversion in the
seabed of the dried sea of Kyushu...

00:02:35.810 --> 00:02:37.830
...the last space battleship Yamato...

00:02:37.830 --> 00:02:40.600
{ISCANDAR}...was about to launch for Iscandar to
obtain the radioactive poison cleaner...

00:02:40.600 --> 00:02:43.700
{ISCANDAR}...a journey of
148,000 light years.

00:02:45.710 --> 00:02:51.920
{SORE}Gamilus noticed and began a large-scale
attack on the wreck of the Yamato.

00:02:54.450 --> 00:02:56.390
The Yamato finally took off.

00:03:03.950 --> 00:03:05.360
That's impossible.

00:03:05.540 --> 00:03:06.710
Unbelievable.

00:03:06.710 --> 00:03:10.600
Shultz, why are
you so confused ?

00:03:10.600 --> 00:03:12.050
Lord Desler.

00:03:12.050 --> 00:03:14.390
Don't be confused by something
as insignificant as the Yamato.

00:03:14.390 --> 00:03:19.700
No matter how they struggle, they have
no chance of leaving the Galactic System.

00:03:21.020 --> 00:03:28.080
My lord, may I have permission to test the
super large missile, and attack the Yamato ?

00:03:28.080 --> 00:03:31.300
A missile target ?

00:03:31.300 --> 00:03:33.550
Very well, proceed.

00:03:33.550 --> 00:03:35.170
Thank you, Lord Desler.

00:03:37.790 --> 00:03:41.380
Gamilus Frontline Base on Pluto

00:03:38.970 --> 00:03:41.720
Super large missile,
begin countdown to launch.

00:03:43.240 --> 00:03:44.570
Target is the Yamato.

00:04:14.520 --> 00:04:16.510
Everyone, listen carefully.

00:04:16.510 --> 00:04:22.570
We're about to begin a journey to Iscandar,
which is a round trip of 296,000 light years.

00:04:22.250 --> 00:04:24.190
Okita Juzo

00:04:22.570 --> 00:04:28.690
Although the space battleship Yamato
is complete, everything is an unknown.

00:04:28.690 --> 00:04:41.190
Gamilus has the ability to attack precisely,
but we can only detect their base on Pluto.

00:04:30.090 --> 00:04:31.200
Kodai Susumu

00:04:31.740 --> 00:04:32.950
Shima Daisuke

00:04:34.800 --> 00:04:36.120
Tokugawa Hikozaemon

00:04:38.760 --> 00:04:40.040
Sanada Shiro

00:04:41.190 --> 00:04:47.950
{SOREWA}That means, there is a definite power
difference between Gamilus and us.

00:04:41.960 --> 00:04:43.130
Mori Yuki

00:04:47.950 --> 00:04:54.850
{SHIKASHI}But we have to return home alive
and save the Earth in one year.

00:04:55.890 --> 00:04:59.500
{SHIKASHI}And I can't
guarantee your safety.

00:05:01.000 --> 00:05:07.350
{SHOKUN}I'll give you a choice. Those who want to
withdraw, please leave during the parade.

00:05:07.350 --> 00:05:09.950
I'll be waiting on the Yamato.  That's all.

00:05:14.400 --> 00:05:15.400
Ten...

00:05:15.400 --> 00:05:16.210
...nine...

00:05:16.210 --> 00:05:17.290
...eight...

00:05:17.290 --> 00:05:18.400
...seven...

00:05:18.400 --> 00:05:19.900
...six...

00:05:19.900 --> 00:05:21.200
...five...

00:05:21.200 --> 00:05:22.290
...four...

00:05:22.290 --> 00:05:23.290
...three...

00:05:23.290 --> 00:05:24.400
...two...

00:05:24.400 --> 00:05:25.800
...one...

00:05:25.800 --> 00:05:27.100
...zero.

00:05:56.220 --> 00:05:58.960
Hey, you aren't going
to escape, are you ?

00:05:58.960 --> 00:06:00.080
You'll go to Iscandar, right ?

00:06:00.080 --> 00:06:02.320
Please, come home safely.

00:06:02.320 --> 00:06:04.510
I wonder if the
Yamato can make it.

00:06:04.510 --> 00:06:07.150
I'm not fully
confident in piloting it.

00:06:07.150 --> 00:06:08.500
Big Brother Daisuke.

00:06:09.040 --> 00:06:09.850
Jiro...

00:06:09.850 --> 00:06:11.080
Daisuke.

00:06:12.160 --> 00:06:13.450
Here.

00:06:13.450 --> 00:06:15.050
Good luck.

00:06:15.050 --> 00:06:16.020
Don't worry.

00:06:16.850 --> 00:06:17.760
Bye.

00:06:21.700 --> 00:06:24.290
Are you going to run away,
leaving your family ?

00:06:24.290 --> 00:06:25.550
How dare you say that ?

00:06:25.550 --> 00:06:30.220
The Yamato is our last hope.
Why don't you cheer them on ?

00:06:30.220 --> 00:06:31.150
How can you...

00:06:32.450 --> 00:06:32.930
Yuki...

00:06:33.400 --> 00:06:34.260
Yuki...

00:06:35.140 --> 00:06:36.150
Yuki...

00:06:38.430 --> 00:06:39.400
Mother.

00:06:39.630 --> 00:06:41.000
Yuki...

00:06:41.000 --> 00:06:44.480
Yuki, do you
have to go ?

00:06:44.480 --> 00:06:45.950
Mother...

00:06:45.950 --> 00:06:50.210
Mother, I won't say goodbye.
I'm just going.

00:06:51.210 --> 00:06:53.550
Father...Father,
please take care.

00:06:54.110 --> 00:06:55.160
Yuki.

00:07:07.780 --> 00:07:09.930
A super large missile
is approaching Earth.

00:07:09.930 --> 00:07:11.850
It seems to have been
launched from Pluto.

00:07:11.850 --> 00:07:13.490
Damn, at a
time like this.

00:07:14.270 --> 00:07:18.320
According to calculations, it will hit
Earth with a 99.9% probability...

00:07:18.320 --> 00:07:20.060
...about 55 minutes from now.

00:07:58.590 --> 00:08:01.340
Captain, everyone is aboard.
No one is missing.

00:08:11.230 --> 00:08:16.400
Jiro, Father,
Mother, watch over me.

00:08:16.400 --> 00:08:17.490
I'll come home.

00:08:17.900 --> 00:08:20.550
Is it alright to make
such an empty promise ?

00:08:21.040 --> 00:08:24.160
You'd better wake up
from that sweet dream.

00:08:24.160 --> 00:08:25.550
Say what ?

00:08:26.150 --> 00:08:30.220
Without question, I'm fully prepared
to risk my life for this mission.

00:08:30.220 --> 00:08:35.730
But once the Yamato launches,
our fate is in Captain Okita's hands.

00:08:35.730 --> 00:08:39.510
Kodai, you don't
trust Captain Okita ?

00:08:39.510 --> 00:08:42.810
Sure, he's had tremendous
achievements in past battles...

00:08:42.810 --> 00:08:45.700
...but many people
died behind him.

00:08:46.600 --> 00:08:47.860
I know, Kodai.

00:08:47.860 --> 00:08:51.480
I was a little hyped up
because of my family's support.

00:08:51.480 --> 00:08:54.400
But your brother
was killed in battle.

00:08:54.400 --> 00:08:57.780
I don't like Captain
Okita's cold-heartedness.

00:09:01.130 --> 00:09:04.530
I'm Kato, and I'll lead the fighter
squadron under your command, Kodai.

00:09:01.730 --> 00:09:03.550
Kato Saburo

00:09:04.250 --> 00:09:06.000
Nanbu Yasuo

00:09:04.530 --> 00:09:06.760
I'm Nanbu, and I'll support
you with the gun combat.

00:09:06.750 --> 00:09:09.000
Aihara Yoshikazu

00:09:06.760 --> 00:09:09.490
I'm Aihara, in charge of communications
under your command, Shima.

00:09:09.490 --> 00:09:11.600
I'm Ohta,
a support pilot.

00:09:09.800 --> 00:09:11.540
Ohta Kenjiro

00:09:12.190 --> 00:09:13.310
Nice to meet you.

00:09:19.500 --> 00:09:22.950
As soon as the energy charge is complete,
we'll leave. Prepare to take off.

00:09:22.950 --> 00:09:25.550
Captain, an energy charge ?

00:09:25.550 --> 00:09:31.450
The engine requires a great amount
of power for the initial activation.

00:09:31.450 --> 00:09:35.400
The entire world is contributing to
make the Yamato's mission successful.

00:09:37.360 --> 00:09:41.850
Kodai, Shima, I'll explain the
arrangement of the ship.  Follow me.

00:09:41.850 --> 00:09:42.690
Aye, sir.

00:09:50.740 --> 00:09:52.040
Turn the ship's schematic on.

00:10:05.330 --> 00:10:09.160
Kodai, that's the weapon
computer under your command.

00:10:16.360 --> 00:10:19.950
It was the commander
and crew's section...

00:10:19.950 --> 00:10:21.400
...but now it's equipped
with the Wave Motion Gun...

00:10:21.400 --> 00:10:24.010
...missile launchers and
its command station.

00:10:26.000 --> 00:10:28.010
Do you know
what this is ?

00:10:29.900 --> 00:10:32.010
This is the muzzle
of the Wave Motion Gun.

00:10:34.810 --> 00:10:38.610
The Wave Motion Gun is the
greatest weapon of the Yamato.

00:10:41.210 --> 00:10:42.950
Just like the
Wave Motion Engine...

00:10:42.950 --> 00:10:46.950
...it uses the energy of tachyon particles,
which exceed the speed of light.

00:11:34.490 --> 00:11:37.550
Oh no, the destination of
the missile has been calculated.

00:11:37.550 --> 00:11:38.830
What ?
Where is it ?

00:11:39.570 --> 00:11:40.860
It's the Yamato.

00:12:06.340 --> 00:12:11.950
I'm Mori Yuki, the Chief of
investigation, analysis and life support.

00:12:11.950 --> 00:12:12.950
Nice to meet you.

00:12:14.770 --> 00:12:19.140
I'm the great doctor Sado.  I'll show you
something interesting, so follow me.

00:12:14.950 --> 00:12:17.950
Sado Sakezo

00:12:19.420 --> 00:12:21.090
This is the
cold sleep room.

00:12:21.090 --> 00:12:24.500
In a long space journeys,
you sometimes lose your temper.

00:12:25.400 --> 00:12:27.880
This's where you can
cool yourself down.

00:12:31.170 --> 00:12:34.790
That Dr. Sado...I wonder if he's
gonna be like that until after take off.

00:12:36.640 --> 00:12:38.810
Next is the resort room.

00:12:45.900 --> 00:12:48.240
Do you want
to join in, guys ?

00:12:48.600 --> 00:12:56.570
It used to be the crew's quarters, but it was
built to create a normal life for the crew.

00:13:00.500 --> 00:13:01.500
W...what the...?

00:13:08.550 --> 00:13:10.300
This is the
Yamato's engineering room.

00:13:10.300 --> 00:13:12.950
All repairs and development
take place in here.

00:13:14.040 --> 00:13:16.760
I'm the chief leader, Sanada.

00:13:16.760 --> 00:13:19.750
The highlight of this room is this
all-purpose manufacturing tool.

00:13:19.750 --> 00:13:22.280
For example, if I want
to build an astro-bike...

00:13:37.420 --> 00:13:38.910
That's a useful machine.

00:13:44.280 --> 00:13:45.810
This is the hangar.

00:13:48.160 --> 00:13:52.910
It was the officers' quarters, as well
as the hangar of the onboard plane.

00:13:54.460 --> 00:13:58.410
Finally, this is the engine room.
There's the powerful Wave Motion engine.

00:13:58.410 --> 00:14:00.220
Oh, welcome.

00:14:01.570 --> 00:14:05.300
I'm Tokugawa,
the chief engineer.

00:14:05.300 --> 00:14:08.610
Boy, this Wave Motion
engine is awesome.

00:14:08.610 --> 00:14:12.060
Wave Motion engine...?
What is it ?

00:14:12.060 --> 00:14:14.080
It's hard to explain simply.

00:14:14.080 --> 00:14:16.950
It compresses the energy in space
and converts it to tachyon particles...

00:14:16.950 --> 00:14:21.000
...which are faster than the speed of light and uses that energy to move.

00:14:21.000 --> 00:14:26.830
{KONO}With this engine, we can travel faster
than light and time. Do you understand ?

00:14:28.000 --> 00:14:32.420
Shima, Kodai, I'm done showing you around
the ship. Let's return to the first bridge.

00:14:33.750 --> 00:14:35.300
Mr. Tokugawa.

00:14:37.160 --> 00:14:39.220
I have a question to ask.

00:14:41.400 --> 00:14:45.080
Mr. Tokugawa, you're almost
always with Captain Okita, right ?

00:14:45.080 --> 00:14:46.350
Yes.

00:14:46.350 --> 00:14:50.200
I want you to tell me frankly.
What kind of person is Captain Okita ?

00:14:50.200 --> 00:14:52.740
Kodai, what's with you ?
You're acting strange.

00:14:53.220 --> 00:14:54.950
Even though he couldn't save
one person, such as my brother...

00:14:54.950 --> 00:14:57.300
...do you think he
can save the Earth ?

00:14:58.750 --> 00:15:02.020
You're the younger brother
of Kodai Mamoru, aren't you ?

00:15:02.790 --> 00:15:07.690
Kodai, you're not the only one who
lost their family.  Don't forget that.

00:15:07.690 --> 00:15:13.600
In fact, Okita lost his
only son in the same battle.

00:15:15.150 --> 00:15:21.550
Even if he only has a one in a million
chance, he'll put his faith in that and act.

00:15:21.550 --> 00:15:25.490
That's how a real man should be.
Isn't that right, Kodai ?

00:15:27.270 --> 00:15:29.300
Even though he couldn't save
one person, such as my brother...

00:15:29.300 --> 00:15:31.110
...do you think he
can save the Earth ?

00:15:41.660 --> 00:15:43.400
Super large missile detected.

00:15:43.400 --> 00:15:46.410
Bearing right 15 degrees,
speed 27 space knots.

00:15:48.420 --> 00:15:49.600
Oh, Kodai.

00:15:49.600 --> 00:15:54.260
A message from Earth Command HQ says that a super large missile is headed for us.

00:15:54.570 --> 00:15:56.330
Oh no, I have to
inform the Captain.

00:16:04.220 --> 00:16:05.380
Kodai Susumu, coming in.

00:16:09.360 --> 00:16:13.530
A super large missile is rapidly approaching.
Please come to the first bridge.

00:16:13.530 --> 00:16:14.500
I see.

00:16:18.460 --> 00:16:19.530
Kodai.

00:16:19.530 --> 00:16:20.840
Sir ?

00:16:24.430 --> 00:16:25.650
It's alright.

00:16:35.780 --> 00:16:37.240
Sub-engines are ready.

00:16:37.240 --> 00:16:38.690
Main engine is
ready for contact.

00:16:38.690 --> 00:16:40.840
Energy charge
100% completed.

00:16:42.300 --> 00:16:44.550
Alright, I'm starting the engine.

00:16:44.550 --> 00:16:45.430
Wait.

00:16:50.150 --> 00:16:55.900
The Wave Motion engine can be started only
once. If we fail, there'll be no second chance.

00:16:56.540 --> 00:17:01.060
Captain, if we hesitate, we'll be blown up by
that super large missile. Is it alright with you ?

00:17:02.060 --> 00:17:06.340
Kodai, if the activation of the main engine
fails, all our weapons will be inaccessible.

00:17:06.340 --> 00:17:08.980
Tokugawa, charge it up
as much as possible.

00:17:08.980 --> 00:17:09.880
Aye, sir.

00:17:11.060 --> 00:17:14.240
Message from Earth Command HQ,
asking if the Yamato is ready yet ?

00:17:16.650 --> 00:17:17.890
Tell them to wait.

00:17:28.470 --> 00:17:31.600
The super large missile will
reach Earth in 600 seconds.

00:17:31.600 --> 00:17:35.040
We only have 10 minutes.
Has the Yamato taken off ?

00:17:35.040 --> 00:17:36.330
No report, sir.

00:17:37.740 --> 00:17:39.860
Energy charge 120%.

00:17:41.260 --> 00:17:43.500
Shima, start the sub-engines.

00:17:43.500 --> 00:17:44.420
Aye, sir.

00:17:45.240 --> 00:17:46.310
Starting sub-engines.

00:17:47.320 --> 00:17:48.810
Engine output 100...

00:17:48.810 --> 00:17:49.940
...200...

00:17:49.940 --> 00:17:51.270
...300...

00:17:51.270 --> 00:17:52.330
...600...

00:17:52.330 --> 00:17:53.770
...1200...

00:17:53.770 --> 00:17:55.080
...2000...

00:17:55.080 --> 00:17:56.550
...2500...

00:17:56.550 --> 00:17:58.950
...2900, 3000.

00:17:58.950 --> 00:18:00.490
Connecting to the
Wave Motion engine circuit.

00:18:20.750 --> 00:18:22.640
Captain, it's not moving !

00:18:24.340 --> 00:18:26.090
Check it again.

00:18:28.410 --> 00:18:29.900
Sub-engines started.

00:18:35.950 --> 00:18:39.530
Captain, I'm sorry.
The synchronal switch was off.

00:18:39.530 --> 00:18:41.100
Oh, c'mon.

00:18:41.350 --> 00:18:44.290
Sub-output 3000,
connecting to the main.

00:19:03.270 --> 00:19:04.850
It's not moving !

00:19:04.850 --> 00:19:06.020
Shut up !

00:19:38.660 --> 00:19:39.860
You did it.

00:19:39.860 --> 00:19:41.260
Moving...
It's moving.

00:19:41.630 --> 00:19:43.020
Wave Motion engine activated.

00:19:44.030 --> 00:19:45.200
Contact.

00:19:45.200 --> 00:19:46.150
Contact.

00:19:48.960 --> 00:19:50.960
It'll reach
Earth in 5 minutes.

00:19:52.920 --> 00:19:54.320
Increasing the power.

00:19:54.990 --> 00:19:56.120
Prepare to take off.

00:19:56.770 --> 00:19:57.710
Preparing to take off.

00:19:58.850 --> 00:20:01.000
Prepare the main guns.

00:20:02.200 --> 00:20:03.380
Preparing the main guns.

00:20:07.880 --> 00:20:09.120
Yamato, take off !

00:20:10.240 --> 00:20:11.420
Yamato, taking off.

00:20:59.590 --> 00:21:01.230
Turn starboard
15 degrees.

00:21:01.230 --> 00:21:02.600
Turning starboard 15 degrees.

00:21:09.420 --> 00:21:12.420
Shock guns' power linked.
Targeting complete.

00:21:12.420 --> 00:21:13.650
Automatic tracking ready.

00:21:15.590 --> 00:21:18.340
Error correction right
1 degree, up 3 degrees.

00:21:18.340 --> 00:21:19.710
Target is on
the Yamato's course.

00:21:22.710 --> 00:21:23.330
Fire.

00:21:23.800 --> 00:21:24.770
Firing.

00:21:44.730 --> 00:21:46.060
Yamato...

00:23:04.500 --> 00:23:12.080
Even if his chance is only one in a
million, he'll put his faith in that and act.

00:23:12.080 --> 00:23:14.450
That's how a
real man should be.

00:23:19.210 --> 00:23:22.080
Kodai, the battle
has just begun.

00:23:22.080 --> 00:23:23.200
Yes, sir.

00:23:25.050 --> 00:23:27.650
The space battleship
Yamato took off.

00:23:27.650 --> 00:23:33.330
Off on a journey of 296,000 light years,
which mankind has never accomplished.

00:23:33.330 --> 00:23:39.010
The space battleship Yamato will head for
Iscandar carrying the hopes of mankind.

00:23:39.010 --> 00:23:42.390
But their time is limited.

00:23:40.410 --> 00:23:47.050
363 days left

00:23:42.390 --> 00:23:46.970
Life on Earth will end in 363 days.

00:23:50.590 --> 00:23:56.270
Okita Juzo:

00:23:50.590 --> 00:23:56.270
Naya Goro

00:23:56.560 --> 00:24:02.280
Mori Yuki:

00:23:56.560 --> 00:24:02.280
Asagami Yoko

00:24:02.560 --> 00:24:08.290
Nanbu Yasuo:

00:24:02.560 --> 00:24:08.290
Kamura Tokio

00:24:09.150 --> 00:24:18.650
Anime Note:
From ep. 3, the beginning of the opening is covered with blue paraffin to match the night scene of ep. 2.

00:24:18.650 --> 00:24:28.650
Note:
Yamato took off once, thanks to Shima and the engineering staff, but to avoid loading the crew from the contaminated surface, it was put back down.  The crew got onboard from the bottom of the third bridge in ep. 3.

00:24:28.650 --> 00:24:38.650
Note:
Okita and the other two were not wearing airtight suits inside the tip of the Wave Motion gun.  Sci-Fi fanatics insist that the Yamato must be protected by an invisible air barrier, but you know...

00:24:38.650 --> 00:24:44.650
History Note:
The launch of Earth's last spaceship, the Yamato, took place on Oct. 9, 2199,
363 days till the extinction of mankind.

00:24:45.180 --> 00:24:51.780
Translation

00:24:45.180 --> 00:24:51.780
Editing

00:24:51.780 --> 00:24:59.350
Timing

00:24:51.780 --> 00:24:59.350
Song Translations

00:24:59.350 --> 00:25:04.300
A
